    use yoagent::types::AgentTool;
  + 
  + /// Marks a tool error as a *deterministic refusal*: the tool declined by policy, so
  + /// re-running the identical request produces the identical answer. Read by
  + /// `prompt_retry::is_deterministic_tool_error` — one definition, two readers, so a
  + /// reworded refusal cannot silently desync from the classifier that recognises it.
  + ///
  + /// Only policy guards carry this marker (read/plan mode, session cap, directory
  + /// denial). Genuine execution failures — a missing file, a cancelled call, an inner
  + /// tool's own error — must NOT carry it: those may well succeed on a retry.
